From: SK-D840N contributors
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: provide the deferred blktrans hook when block support is off

The generic 402-mtd-blktrans-call-add-disks-after-mtd-device.patch adds an
unconditional call from mtdcore to register_mtd_blktrans_devs(). Its
implementation is in mtd_blkdevs.o, built only with CONFIG_MTD_BLKDEVS.
SK-D840N intentionally disables both MTD_BLOCK and MTD_BLOCK_RO, so a
character-device-only MTD build otherwise fails at the vmlinux link.

Provide an empty inline hook when the translation layer is disabled. Use
MTD_BLKDEVS, not one of its individual users, and keep the existing external
hook for enabled configurations. No block interface or flash write path is
enabled by this target-local follow-up to the generic patch. This does not
redesign the generic patch's module loading or symbol export behavior.

--- a/include/linux/mtd/blktrans.h
+++ b/include/linux/mtd/blktrans.h
@@ -76,7 +76,14 @@ extern int deregister_mtd_blktrans(struct mtd_blktrans_ops *tr);
 extern int add_mtd_blktrans_dev(struct mtd_blktrans_dev *dev);
 extern int del_mtd_blktrans_dev(struct mtd_blktrans_dev *dev);
 extern int mtd_blktrans_cease_background(struct mtd_blktrans_dev *dev);
+
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MTD_BLKDEVS)
 extern void register_mtd_blktrans_devs(void);
+#else
+static inline void register_mtd_blktrans_devs(void)
+{
+}
+#endif
 
 /**
  * module_mtd_blktrans() - Helper macro for registering a mtd blktrans driver
